Sources of the Maine RCV corpus and their terms of use, as read on 2026-11-10

The repository holds no file of the corpus.  It holds each file's URL, size, and SHA-256 in
manifest.json and the figures of the summary reports that recount.py holds.  fetch.py downloads
each file from its URL in the manifest into a local directory that Git ignores, or checks a file
saved there from a web browser.

Maine Department of the Secretary of State, Bureau of Corporations, Elections and Commissions

The RCV summary reports, the first-choice results, the cast vote record spreadsheets, the 2026
primary candidate list, and the list of candidate withdrawals of May 22, 2026 come from the
Secretary of State's election results pages,
https://www.maine.gov/sos/elections-voting/election-results-data and
https://www.maine.gov/sos/elections-voting/election-results-data/election-results-2024.  21-A
M.R.S. section 723-A, subsection 5-C, at
https://legislature.maine.gov/statutes/21-A/title21-Asec723-A.html, states: "The Secretary of
State shall post the complete cast vote record on its publicly accessible website as soon as the
certified results are reported."  On 2026-11-10 www.maine.gov returned HTTP 403 to scripted
requests for both pages, for the Secretary of State's home page https://www.maine.gov/sos/, and for
the Maine.gov policies, https://www.maine.gov/portal/policies/index.html, and content disclaimer,
https://www.maine.gov/portal/policies/disclaimer.html, so no terms of the site are quoted here.
